course: dictionary
lesson: 2305
title: One word, three meanings: critically
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Critically» can mean very seriously, it can mean judging carefully, and it can mean finding fault. The words around it show you which meaning the writer chose.
explain: «Sawfish are critically endangered, mainly because their saws tangle in fishing nets.» The clue is endangered, a word about risk. So critically means very seriously, at high risk of dying out.
explain: When critically is next to thinking or speaking, it changes. «She spoke critically of the plan» means she found faults in it. Check by swapping your meaning in: «She spoke very seriously of the plan» does not fit, but «She found faults in the plan» does.
fact: Critically means very seriously or dangerously, as in «critically endangered».
fact: Critically means judging carefully what is good and bad, as in think critically.
fact: Critically means in a way that finds fault, as in «she spoke critically of the plan».
fact: «Critically endangered» means at very high risk of dying out, as with the Sumatran tiger and the kakapo.
fact: Critical thinking means asking: is it true, who says so, and how do they know? This helps spot fake news.
exercise: «Sawfish are critically endangered, mainly because their saws tangle in fishing nets.» What does critically mean here? | Judging carefully what is good and bad | In a way that finds fault | *Very seriously, at high risk | Very quietly
exercise: Mrs Patel says, «We must think critically about every news story.» What does critically mean here? | Very quickly | In a way that finds fault with people | *Judging carefully: is it true, and how do they know? | Very seriously ill
exercise: «She spoke critically of the plan.» What does critically mean here? | Very seriously at risk | Judging carefully what is good and bad | In a friendly way | *In a way that finds fault
test: «The Chinese giant salamander is the largest amphibian in the world, and is critically endangered from hunting and changed rivers.» Which word is the clue that critically means very seriously? | Largest | Metres | *Endangered | Amphibian
test: Ella reads an advert and asks, «Is it true, who says so, and how do they know?» Which meaning of critically fits this skill? | Very slowly | Very seriously at high risk | *Judging carefully what is good and bad | In a way that finds fault
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The class had to think critically about the advert»? | *Judging carefully what is good and bad | Very seriously, at high risk | Finding fault in a rude way | Very quickly
